.TH ZVM-RUN 1 "August 2026" "ZVM v0.9.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zvm-run \- run Zig without changing the active version
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zvm run
.RI [ version ]
.RI [ zig-arguments ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run the Zig executable from
.I version
with the remaining arguments.
Running an already installed version leaves the selected version unchanged.
.PP
If the requested version is not installed, ZVM offers to install it.
Accepting this prompt installs it as the global default before running it.
Version shorthand and aliases are accepted; see
.BR zvm (1).
.PP
When no version is supplied, ZVM reads
.B .minimum_zig_version
from
.I build.zig.zon
in the current directory and passes all arguments to Zig.
For example,
.B zvm run build --help
uses the project's minimum Zig version.
.PP
Arguments after
.I version
are passed directly to Zig, including arguments beginning with a hyphen.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
zvm run 0.13.0 version
zvm run .14 build test
zvm run master build run -- --port 8080
zvm run build --help
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zvm (1),
.BR zig (1),
.BR zvm-install (1),
.BR zvm-use (1)
